### Handle a return waiting for review

Some returns wait for the merchant's review before Skroutz schedules them: a faulty product, a
missing part, or a withdrawal or wrong size outside the return policy. Such a return is in state
`pending_merchant_review` and carries a [`review`](#review) with its deadline and the
[`handle_options`](#handle-options) it accepts.

Send one of the `handle_options` as `option`, with the params it takes. The response is the
updated return.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/handle
</pre>

Option | Params
------ | ------
`approve` | None
A rejection reason, e.g. `not_faulty` | `comment`, required when the option's `comment_required` is `true`, up to 1000 characters. `proposed_part_url`, optional and only when the option's `supports_proposed_part_url` is `true`: a link on Skroutz to the part, e.g. when it is sold separately
`send_missing_part` | See [Send the missing part](#send-the-missing-part)

Every option resolves the review, so the return leaves `pending_merchant_review` (e.g. to `rejected`
after a rejection) and Skroutz sends a [return updated](/smart_cart/returns_webhook#return-updated) webhook.

#### Example: approve

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/handle \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "option": "approve" }'
</pre>

#### Example: reject

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/handle \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "option": "not_faulty", "comment": "The product works according to its specifications." }'
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_returns_handle %>

#### Send the missing part

For a `missing_part` review, the merchant can send the missing part to the customer instead of
receiving the product back. Skroutz creates an additional delivery of the part, at the shop's
cost, and the return moves to `resolved_without_return`: the product is not returned.

Pick the values from the option's [`delivery`](#delivery-options), as when
[accepting an order](/smart_cart/orders_api#accept-a-single-order). All params are required.

Param               | Type    | Description
------------------- | ------- | -----------
`pickup_location`   | String  | The `id` of one of the `delivery.pickup_location`
`cargo`             | Boolean | `true` to book the cargo carrier, using the location's `cargo_pickup_window`. `false` otherwise, using its `pickup_window`
`pickup_window`     | String  | The `id` of one of the chosen list's windows. The window books its own courier
`weight`            | Integer | Kilos, within `delivery.weight`
`number_of_parcels` | Integer | One of `delivery.number_of_parcels`
`items_description` | String  | What is being sent, up to 250 characters
`delivery_reason`   | String  | Why it is being sent, up to 250 characters

A window that is no longer available is rejected, never replaced with another one. Fetch the
return again for the current windows: the windows in a webhook payload are those available when
it was sent.

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/handle \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{
    "option": "send_missing_part",
    "pickup_location": "YlpD0KROym",
    "cargo": false,
    "pickup_window": "20261029T1000-20261029T1400",
    "weight": 2,
    "number_of_parcels": 1,
    "items_description": "Mounting accessories",
    "delivery_reason": "Sending the missing part"
  }'
</pre>

#### Handle errors

Status | Code | When
------ | ---- | ----
`400`  | `ParameterMissing` | `option` is missing
`404`  | `return_error` | The return does not exist or does not belong to your shop
`422`  | `review_state` | The return is not waiting for your review: it was already handled, its deadline passed, or it never needed one
`422`  | `option` | The return does not offer this option, e.g. `contact_customer`
`422`  | The param's name, e.g. `comment`, `pickup_window` | The param is missing or invalid

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "pickup_window",
      "messages": [
        "is not an available pickup window"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

### Submit the inspection of an item

A faulty product the customer sent back for a technical inspection waits for the merchant's report.
The return is in state `pending_service_inspection`, and each line item waiting for a report carries
an [`inspection`](#inspection) with its deadline and the [options](#inspection-options) it accepts.
A return with several faulty items is inspected item by item.

Send the item's `id` as `item` and one of its `inspection.options` as `option`, with what the option
requires. Send it as `multipart/form-data`, since it carries files. The response is the updated return.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/submit_inspection
</pre>

Param                      | Type    | Description
-------------------------- | ------- | -----------
`item`                     | String  | The `id` of the line item
`option`                   | String  | One of the item's `inspection.options`
`service_report_file`      | File    | The service report, required when the option's `service_report_file_required` is `true`. PNG, JPEG, JPG or PDF, up to 7 MB
`in_stock`                 | Boolean | `true` or `false`: whether you can send the customer a replacement. Required when the option's `in_stock_answer_required` is `true`
`comment`                  | String  | Optional, a comment to the customer, up to 400 characters
`additional_attachments[]` | File    | Optional, up to 5 files for the customer, each PNG, JPEG, JPG or PDF, up to 7 MB. Send the param once per file, with `[]`

Once submitted, the item no longer carries an `inspection`. When no item waits for an inspection,
the return leaves `pending_service_inspection` (e.g. to `returned`) and Skroutz sends a
[return updated](/smart_cart/returns_webhook#return-updated) webhook.

#### Example: free repair under warranty

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/submit_inspection \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -F 'item=gY6oNzr8jp' \
  -F 'option=under_warranty_repairable' \
  -F 'service_report_file=@service_report.pdf' \
  -F 'comment=The charging port was replaced and the tablet tested for 2 hours.' \
  -F 'additional_attachments[]=@photo_1.jpg' \
  -F 'additional_attachments[]=@photo_2.jpg'
</pre>

#### Example: replacement under warranty, out of stock

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/submit_inspection \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -F 'item=gY6oNzr8jp' \
  -F 'option=under_warranty_unrepairable' \
  -F 'in_stock=false' \
  -F 'service_report_file=@service_report.pdf'
</pre>

#### Response

<%= render_code '{
  "return": {
    "return_code": "R-111111-1111111",
    "state": "returned",
    "order_code": "48213907",
    "created_at": "2026-08-18T09:12:03Z",
    "return_line_items": [
      {
        "id": "gY6oNzr8jp",
        "ean": "1234567890123",
        "product_name": "Apple iPad 10.9 64GB",
        "returning_quantity": 1,
        "return_reason": "faulty",
        "requested_compensation": "repair",
        "user_comment": "The tablet does not charge."
      }
    ]
  }
}', 'javascript' %>

#### Inspection errors

Status | Code | When
------ | ---- | ----
`400`  | `ParameterMissing` | `item` or `option` is missing
`404`  | `return_error` | The return does not exist or does not belong to your shop
`422`  | `item` | The return has no such item
`422`  | `inspection_state` | The item is not waiting for your inspection: it has none, it was already submitted, or Skroutz handles it
`422`  | `option` | The item does not offer this option
`422`  | The param's name, e.g. `in_stock`, `service_report_file`, `additional_attachments` | The param is missing or invalid

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "in_stock",
      "messages": [
        "must be answered for the selected service outcome"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

### Watch a customer video

The `url` and `thumbnail_url` of a line item's [`user_videos`](#user-videos) point to the
following endpoints. Each takes your API token and redirects to the video's player page or its
thumbnail image, on a link signed for a short time. Request them when you need to show the video,
rather than storing the link they redirect to.

<pre class="terminal">
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/videos/:id
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/videos/:id/thumbnail
</pre>

Status | When
------ | ----
`302`  | Redirects to the player page or the thumbnail
`404`  | The video does not exist, is not yet uploaded, or does not belong to your return
`429`  | More than 60 video requests in a minute
`503`  | The video could not be signed. Try again later

## Error handling

In case of errors, the response will have a representative HTTP status code
in the `4xx` range. The body would contain an array of `errors`.

For example, if the requested return code does not exist (or does not belong to your shop),
you will get a `404` HTTP status code (Not Found):

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "not_found",
      "messages": [
        "Return not found"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

